.TH "CSSROTATE.ANGLE" "3JS" "September 10, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSRotate.angle \- CSSRotate: angle property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]angle\f[B]\f[R] property of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R]
interface represents the angle of rotation.
A positive angle denotes a clockwise rotation, a negative angle a
counter\-clockwise one.
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R]
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Reading and setting the angle
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] rotate = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSRotate(CSS.deg(45));

console.log(rotate.angle.value); \f[I]// 45\f[R]
console.log(rotate.angle.unit); \f[I]// \(dqdeg\(dq\f[R]

rotate.angle = CSS.deg(90);
console.log(rotate.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqrotate(90deg)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
